@startuml
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam roundcorner 14
skinparam ArrowColor #334155
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.8
skinparam titleFontSize 19
skinparam titleFontStyle bold

title Integrity Controls — Four Independent Locks on Data Accuracy

rectangle "1. ONE IDENTITY,\nTWO DOORS" as C1 #DBEAFE {
  component "The same sign-in works\nfor changing and for enquiring" as C1A
}
rectangle "2. SEPARATE GATEWAYS" as C2 #DCFCE7 {
  component "Read and change traffic\nare physically distinct paths" as C2A
}
rectangle "3. DATABASE-LEVEL LOCK" as C3 #FEF3C7 {
  component "The read path carries a\npermanently read-only identity" as C3A
}
rectangle "4. AUTOMATED PROOF" as C4 #FCE7F3 {
  component "A repeatable test asserts\nthe guarantee every run" as C4A
}

C1 -[#0EA5E9]-> C2
C2 -[#22C55E]-> C3
C3 -[#F59E0B]-> C4

note bottom of C3 #FFFBEB
  The lock sits **in the database**, not in a
  configuration file. If any component above is
  ever misconfigured, the database still refuses
  the change. Controls that sit next to the risk
  are not controls.
end note

note bottom of C4 #FDF2F8
  Guarantees are only real if they are
  **tested on demand**. A single command
  re-proves the whole set, and is treated
  as a release gate.
end note

@enduml